# Gitignored live file is `.env` next to this repo, or
# `/config/hungarian-transport/.env` on Home Assistant.
# GitHub Actions reads only BAHART_GTFS_URL, MOBILITY_DATABASE_REFRESH_TOKEN
# and TRANSITLAND_API_KEY, as repository secrets of the same names. The MAV_*
# settings are local only: the release build has no MÁV feed. The city guard
# escape hatch is the repository *variable* HUNGARIAN_TRANSPORT_ALLOW_MISSING
# (every run, with a warning), plus the workflow input allow_missing (one run,
# added to the variable).
#
# Do not commit real values. Public CI falls back to menetbrand.
# MÁV rail GTFS is registration-only; keep the zip local (gitignored).
# Downloads use https: an http:// URL here is fetched as https://, and so is
# its daily fingerprint check (HEAD). A redirect from https to plain http on
# the same host is asked over https again; any other redirect to plain http
# is refused. Only the city feeds marked "insecure" in build_city_index.py
# may use http (HEAD, fallback download, a redirect).
#
# Lines may read `export KEY=value`; a ` # comment` after a value is ignored.
# On Home Assistant this file wins over /config/.env. HUNGARIAN_TRANSPORT_WWW
# (served folder) and HUNGARIAN_TRANSPORT_WEBHOOK (where the update reports) may
# be set here as well.

BAHART_GTFS_URL=
MOBILITY_DATABASE_REFRESH_TOKEN=
TRANSITLAND_API_KEY=
# When set, mav-gtfs.zip in the working folder (/config/hungarian-transport on
# Home Assistant) is this URL's copy, downloaded again once it is 20 hours old.
MAV_GTFS_URL=
MAV_GTFS_ZIP=
# Unzipped pfaedle output (OSM-matched rails). Preferred over the official zip.
MAV_PFAEDLE_DIR=
# City feed ids (comma-separated, or "all") a rebuild may lose against the
# index it replaces. Leave empty: a missing feed then keeps the old index. A
# feed whose timetable has ended in the old index as well (Bahart out of
# season, several feeds at year end) needs no entry: only trips that still
# run count, feed by feed.
HUNGARIAN_TRANSPORT_ALLOW_MISSING=
